# E §3.1 The order of the checks (tally 2.1.2, issue #23): in the items' own checks, "one sort at a time ... each by
# full path and line". Two moves each refuse their `on` (a date in a rule, LOAD-LITERAL); zz is written first, so its
# refusal prints, though aa comes first by id (tally 2.1.1's refcore took moves by id and printed aa's, line 17).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

move zz: transfers
  on 2026-01-10

move aa: transfers
  on 2026-02-10

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL a date in a rule; make it a version (m.tally:14)
